post_content:
I... need to issue an apology to Facebook Marketplace. FBMP? I slept on you for far too long. Did my opinions get shaped by one absolutely insane posting experience I had in 2019 when trying to get rid of an ikea futon? Yes. Have they further been shaped by the fact that buying new furniture is now absurdly expensive and takes forever — what do you MEAN this sectional costs $7,500 and takes 12-48 weeks to ship??? Sure have. But... I’ve recently discovered that it’s kinda the best? Like when I needed to get rid of 12 boxes of packing peanuts and posted them for free and within 10 minutes they were gone? Or when I went to buy a $50 bench last week and the sweet older gent who MADE IT BY HAND decided to give it to me for $25 and asked if I wanted a second one for free? Honestly my world has been changed and I am excited for this next chapter #bless
And now, a BALLIN’ on a BUDGET roundup for my thrifty friends out there. HAPPY THURSDAY FAM, HOPE IT’S A GREAT ONE! 
@jbrylah 
@simonreah 
Blackwood Community Posting
Credit/ lethalityjane
@theapebrigade e 
@ewdatsgross & @hashjennii 
@wittyotter

