I kind of always thought that friendship was a naturally occurring thing and that the people in my life who were my friends would always just be there. But that was a lot easier when we had 5 classes together every week and hosted parties every night? In my late 30s, I’ve realized that keeping friendships going takes some work, and making new friends takes even more work. That friendship isn’t just going to happen if you don’t make an effort to put yourself out there, let people know you think they’re cool, invite them to do things, and be vulnerable *pukes*. It’s true. And it’s hard. But I’m working on it. 
Last week I shared some of our recent Single of the Day features in a dating roundup. Today? I’m sharing some of our recent Friend of the Day features in a FRIENDSHIP roundup (awwWWwwWWW). These are real people who are putting themselves out there looking for friendships (+ a few are Friend AND Single of the day features) - looking for new friends? Your new bestie just may be in this very carousel. SWIPE! 
And now, a FRIENDSHIP roundup to brighten that Thursday feed. Thanks for being here, friends! Appreciate each and every last one of you. Hope your day is a magical one
