Book thoughts in no particular order: 
-I fell hard for the movie Project Hail Mary. It healed a part of me I didn’t know was broken. I somehow ended up seeing it in theaters THREE TIMES and am currently knitting a sweater that Ryan Gosling wore in the movie??? (smdh times are weird fam we do what we gotta do to make it through) I decided to read the book Project Hail Mary and am so glad I did, it’s great... maybe the best book to movie adaptation I’ve ever come across. I’m honestly not sure if I’m sad I didn’t read it first? The movie was such a magical experience, going in with zero expectations and having such a great time in the theater, and I still really enjoyed the book. But reading 500 pages of a story you already know is definitely a bigger commitment than a 2 hour movie of a story you already know? Thoughts?? 
-A friend was recently making the point that while she loves libraries, she is too germaphobic to check out hard copy library books and has a library card exclusively for e books and audiobooks, making the point that holding a paper book that countless strangers have brought to bed with them, read while on the toilet, read while eating, etc. etc. etc. is too icky to consider. I had never thought of this and am not sure what to make of it. I’d also love your thoughts here, plz. 
-Finally- my book recs are on the final slide, and I’d love yours too! I recently bought this little device that blocks social media on my phone when I tap it, and have stopped scrolling after 5 pm. Game changer. I’m reading more than ever and have never been happier - add to my to read pile! 
And now, a BOOK roundup to make that Monday morning feed 1/10th of the way to a FREE PERSONAL PAN PIZZA!!!!! WAHOOOOOOO! (love you mean it glad you’re here, friend) 
@alessandra_ranelli 
