My childhood neighbor who worked at an advertising agency and got a ton of free things gave me a No Fear hat when I was a kid and told me that each one was unique because of the saying under the rim of the hat and that they were absolutely impossible to find because they were just *so* popular. Embracing it with the passion I had for 90s things that I really had no interest in for any reason other than that they were hard to find (see tickle me elmo, beanie babies, Et. al), I wore that hat every single day, proudly showing anyone who asked (and many who did not) the unique saying that was under *my* hat which read “Beaten paths are for beaten men.” What a timeline. 
The 90s were simpler times. Take me back.
And now, a *~90~*’s baby roundup to start off that Friday feed in a way that’s DRIPPING WITH NOSTALGIA, because that’s always a fun way to round out the week. XOXO THANK’S FOR BEING HERE FRIENDS- you’re all tubular. 
#meme #memesdaily #memes #nostalgia 
@nikkilimo 
Credit/ facetedcarapace
